rf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the LaPorte County record runs 75 years back to 1951 across 8 grids. On the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids, January to February and November to December each came in under 90% of normal in 35 years, the most of any pair. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 46% of normal in January to February and 67% in April to May. Grid 25373 had its driest year in 1956 at 71%, and the other grids bottomed out in 1953, 1962 or 1963.</p>"}
